@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+The mask and the uncertainty of a `~sunpy.map.GenericMap` are now carried through the operations that build a new map from it: `~sunpy.map.GenericMap.submap`, `~sunpy.map.GenericMap.resample`, `~sunpy.map.GenericMap.rotate`, `~sunpy.map.GenericMap.superpixel`, `~sunpy.map.GenericMap.shift_reference_coord`, `~sunpy.map.GenericMap.reproject_to`, and arithmetic between a map and a number or a quantity.
+Masked pixels no longer take part in an interpolation, an uncertainty is propagated as a variance and keeps the kind it was stored in, and `~sunpy.map.MapSequence` has gained an ``uncertainty`` property alongside its existing ``mask``.
